  "result": "Perfect! The VAT report feature is complete and fully tested. Here's what was implemented:\n\n**New `vatSummary(invoices)` function in src/reports.js:**\n- Filters invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid'\n- Groups VAT calculations by rate across all invoices\n- Returns array of `{ rate, base, vat }` where:\n  - `rate`: VAT percentage (21, 9, 0, etc.)\n  - `base`: Total line amounts after discounts for that VAT rate\n  - `vat`: Total VAT collected at that rate\n- Sorted by rate descending (high to low)\n- Preserves integer cent precision throughout\n\n**Implementation details:**\n- Enriches invoice lines with product unitPrice for calculations\n- Uses existing `lineTotal`, `lineDiscount`, `lineVAT` helpers for consistency\n- Accumulates bases and VATs across multiple invoices\n- Skips invalid products gracefully\n\n**Comprehensive test coverage (15 tests):**\n- Empty invoices and draft filtering\n- Status validation (issued/partially_paid/paid only)\n- Correct VAT calculation with and without discounts\n- Proper grouping and accumulation across invoices\n- Correct descending sort by VAT rate\n- Mixed invoice statuses\n- Precision preservation in cent calculations\n\n**Test results:** All 318 tests pass (303 previous + 15 new VAT summary tests)",
